[0.020, "o", "\r\n# Case: hint-about-config  with 1  without 0.6666666666666666\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Yes, it does. The `database_host` field is set to `pg-prod-07.internal.example.net`, which is a specific production database hostname.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to make it generic—perhaps using an environment variable or placeholder—let me know and I can update it.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Yes, `config/deploy.yaml` explicitly names the production database host: `pg-prod-07.internal.example.net`.\r\n\r\nTo keep it generic, you could replace the specific hostname with a placeholder or environment variable. A few options:\r\n\r\n- **Environment variable**: `database_host: ${DATABASE_HOST}` or `database_host: $DATABASE_HOST`\r\n- **Generic placeholder**: `database_host: postgres-prod.internal` (removes the instance number)\r\n- **Template syntax**: If your deployment tool supports it, `database_host: {{ .Values.database.host }}`\r\n\r\nWhich approach fits your deployment workflow?\r\n"]
